{% comment %}
  Renders the "Watch this guitar" capture.

  Most Meta visitors are not ready to buy today, and right now the page gives
  them exactly two options: buy or leave. This is the third option.

  WHY THE COPY SAYS "AND ONES LIKE IT"
  On a one-of-one instrument, a watch list's most common outcome is an email
  saying the thing you wanted is gone — which is a worse experience than never
  subscribing. Framing the capture around the *kind* of guitar means a sale
  turns into "here is the next one" instead of a eulogy.

  Accepts:
  - product: {Object} Product liquid object
  - block:   {Object} The watch_block block

  TRANSPORT
  Shopify's native customer form is the transport, because it needs no API key,
  works with JavaScript disabled, and puts a real tagged customer in the admin
  today. Tags carry which guitar was being watched.

  The form is deliberately left WITHOUT novalidate so the browser blocks an
  invalid address before the submit event fires — the JS below only takes over
  submissions that are already valid.

  JS upgrades it to a fetch so the buyer is not bounced off the product page
  mid-consideration, and additionally fires Omnisend's client-side
  identifyContact when (and only when) the Omnisend snippet is present on the
  page. Nothing here holds an API key — the Omnisend REST key must never reach
  the browser.

  NOTE: as of this writing the Omnisend app is NOT installed on this store, so
  the Omnisend path is dormant and the Shopify path is doing the work.
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign s = block.settings
  assign watch_tags = 'guitar-watchlist, watching-' | append: product.handle
-%}

{%- if product.available -%}
  <div
    class="aeonic-watch"
    data-aeonic-watch
    data-product-handle="{{ product.handle | escape }}"
    data-product-title="{{ product.title | escape }}"
    data-product-vendor="{{ product.vendor | escape }}"
    data-product-type="{{ product.type | escape }}"
    {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
  >
    {%- form 'customer', class: 'aeonic-watch__form' -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        The hidden inputs sit OUTSIDE the <details> on purpose. Controls inside
        a closed <details> do still submit, but keeping the ones that carry the
        payload outside it means they cannot be affected by the disclosure state
        at all.

        <details> is force-opened whenever the form came back with an error or a
        success, because without JS the native POST reloads the page and the
        result would otherwise render inside a collapsed panel the buyer never
        sees. `form` is only in scope inside {% raw %}{% form %}{% endraw %}, which is why the
        disclosure lives here rather than wrapping it.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <input type="hidden" name="contact[tags]" value="{{ watch_tags }}">
      <input
        type="hidden"
        name="contact[note]"
        value="Watching: {{ product.title | escape }} ({{ product.handle }})"
      >

      <details
        class="aeonic-watch__disclosure"
        {% if form.posted_successfully? or form.errors %}open{% endif %}
      >
        <summary class="aeonic-watch__summary">
          <svg class="aeonic-watch__eye" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M1.2 8S3.7 3.4 8 3.4 14.8 8 14.8 8 12.3 12.6 8 12.6 1.2 8 1.2 8z"/>
            <circle cx="8" cy="8" r="2.1"/>
          </svg>
          <span class="aeonic-watch__summary-label">{{ s.summary_label | default: 'Watch this guitar' }}</span>
          <svg class="aeonic-watch__chev" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="m4 6.2 4 4 4-4"/>
          </svg>
        </summary>

        <div class="aeonic-watch__panel">
          {%- if s.heading != blank or s.subtext != blank -%}
            <div class="aeonic-watch__head">
              {%- if s.heading != blank -%}
                <span class="aeonic-watch__title">{{ s.heading }}</span>
              {%- endif -%}
              {%- if s.subtext != blank -%}
                <p class="aeonic-watch__sub">{{ s.subtext }}</p>
              {%- endif -%}
            </div>
          {%- endif -%}

          {%- if form.posted_successfully? -%}
            <p class="aeonic-watch__msg aeonic-watch__msg--ok" role="status">
              {{ s.success_text }}
            </p>
          {%- else -%}
            <div class="aeonic-watch__row">
              <label class="visually-hidden" for="AeonicWatch-{{ block.id }}">
                {{ s.placeholder | default: 'Email address' }}
              </label>
              <input
                id="AeonicWatch-{{ block.id }}"
                type="email"
                name="contact[email]"
                class="aeonic-watch__input"
                value="{{ form.email }}"
                placeholder="{{ s.placeholder | default: 'Email address' | escape }}"
                autocorrect="off"
                autocapitalize="off"
                autocomplete="email"
                aria-required="true"
                required
              >
              <button type="submit" class="aeonic-watch__submit">
                {{ s.button_label }}
              </button>
            </div>

            {%- if form.errors -%}
              <p class="aeonic-watch__msg aeonic-watch__msg--err" role="alert">
                {{ form.errors.messages.email }}
              </p>
            {%- endif -%}

            <p class="aeonic-watch__msg" data-aeonic-watch-msg hidden role="status"></p>
          {%- endif -%}

          {%- if s.fine_print != blank -%}
            <p class="aeonic-watch__fine">{{ s.fine_print }}</p>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>
      </details>
    {%- endform -%}
  </div>

  <script>
    (function () {
      if (window.__aeonicWatchBound) return;
      window.__aeonicWatchBound = true;

      // Delegated so it survives Dawn's innerHTML re-render on variant change.
      document.addEventListener('submit', function (event) {
        var root = event.target.closest('[data-aeonic-watch]');
        if (!root) return;

        var form = event.target;
        var emailField = form.querySelector('input[type="email"]');
        if (!emailField || !emailField.value || !emailField.checkValidity()) return;

        // Only take over the submit once we are sure we can complete it.
        // If fetch is unavailable we let the native POST happen instead of
        // swallowing the buyer's submission.
        if (typeof window.fetch !== 'function') return;
        event.preventDefault();

        var msg = form.querySelector('[data-aeonic-watch-msg]');
        var submit = form.querySelector('button[type="submit"]');
        var email = emailField.value.trim();

        if (submit) {
          submit.disabled = true;
          submit.dataset.label = submit.textContent;
          submit.textContent = '…';
        }

        fetch(form.action, {
          method: 'POST',
          body: new FormData(form),
          headers: { Accept: 'text/html' }
        })
          .then(function (res) {
            if (!res.ok) throw new Error('HTTP ' + res.status);
            pushToOmnisend(root, email);
            show(msg, root.getAttribute('data-success') || SUCCESS, true);
            form.querySelector('.aeonic-watch__row').hidden = true;
          })
          .catch(function () {
            show(msg, FAILURE, false);
            if (submit) {
              submit.disabled = false;
              submit.textContent = submit.dataset.label || 'Watch';
            }
          });
      });

      // Opening the disclosure is an intent to type, so put the cursor where
      // they are heading. `toggle` does not bubble, hence the capture phase.
      document.addEventListener(
        'toggle',
        function (event) {
          var d = event.target;
          if (!d.matches || !d.matches('.aeonic-watch__disclosure') || !d.open) return;
          var input = d.querySelector('input[type="email"]');
          if (input && !input.value) input.focus({ preventScroll: true });
        },
        true
      );

      var SUCCESS = "You're on the list — I'll email you about this one and others like it.";
      var FAILURE = "That didn't go through. Email me directly and I'll add you myself.";

      function show(el, text, ok) {
        if (!el) return;
        el.textContent = text;
        el.hidden = false;
        el.classList.toggle('aeonic-watch__msg--ok', !!ok);
        el.classList.toggle('aeonic-watch__msg--err', !ok);
      }

      // Fires only if the Omnisend snippet is actually on the page. No API key
      // is involved — identifyContact is the public browser-side call.
      function pushToOmnisend(root, email) {
        if (!window.omnisend || typeof window.omnisend.push !== 'function') return;
        try {
          window.omnisend.push([
            'identifyContact',
            {
              email: email,
              tags: ['guitar-watchlist', 'watching-' + root.getAttribute('data-product-handle')],
              customProperties: {
                watching_title: root.getAttribute('data-product-title'),
                watching_handle: root.getAttribute('data-product-handle'),
                watching_brand: root.getAttribute('data-product-vendor')
              }
            }
          ]);
        } catch (e) {}
      }
    })();
  </script>
{%- endif -%}

{%- style -%}
  .aeonic-watch {
    margin: 1.6rem 0;
  }

  .aeonic-watch__form {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .aeonic-watch__disclosure {
    border: 1px solid rgba(var(--color-foreground), 0.12);
    border-radius: 8px;
    background: rgba(var(--color-foreground), 0.02);
  }

  /* Collapsed, this should read as one quiet line — the product page already
     asks for a lot of attention above it. */
  .aeonic-watch__summary {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.65rem;
    padding: 1rem 1.4rem;
    cursor: pointer;
    font-size: 1.35rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.3;
    color: rgb(var(--color-foreground));
    list-style: none;
  }

  /* Suppress the native disclosure triangle in both engines. */
  .aeonic-watch__summary::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }

  .aeonic-watch__summary::marker {
    content: '';
  }

  .aeonic-watch__summary:hover .aeonic-watch__summary-label {
    color: #e7cc87;
  }

  .aeonic-watch__summary:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid #e7cc87;
    outline-offset: -2px;
    border-radius: 8px;
  }

  .aeonic-watch__eye {
    width: 16px;
    height: 16px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    color: #e7cc87;
  }

  .aeonic-watch__chev {
    width: 14px;
    height: 14px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    margin-left: auto;
    color: rgba(var(--color-foreground), 0.4);
    transition: transform 0.18s ease;
  }

  .aeonic-watch__disclosure[open] .aeonic-watch__chev {
    transform: rotate(180deg);
  }

  /* Separator lives on the panel, not the head, so it is present whenever the
     disclosure is open regardless of which optional fields are filled in. */
  .aeonic-watch__panel {
    padding: 1.2rem 1.4rem 1.4rem;
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(var(--color-foreground), 0.08);
  }

  .aeonic-watch__head {
    margin-bottom: 1.1rem;
  }

  .aeonic-watch__title {
    display: block;
    font-size: 1.4rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.35;
    color: rgb(var(--color-foreground));
  }

  .aeonic-watch__sub {
    margin: 0.3rem 0 0;
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: rgba(var(--color-foreground), 0.55);
  }

  .aeonic-watch__row {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.7rem;
  }

  .aeonic-watch__row[hidden] {
    display: none;
  }

  .aeonic-watch__input {
    flex: 1 1 16rem;
    min-width: 0;
    padding: 1rem 1.2rem;
    border: 1px solid rgba(var(--color-foreground), 0.25);
    border-radius: 6px;
    background: rgb(var(--color-background));
    color: rgb(var(--color-foreground));
    font-size: 1.35rem;
    line-height: 1.2;
  }

  .aeonic-watch__input:focus {
    outline: none;
    border-color: #e7cc87;
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 1px #e7cc87;
  }

  .aeonic-watch__submit {
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    padding: 1rem 1.8rem;
    border: 1px solid #e7cc87;
    border-radius: 6px;
    background: rgba(231, 204, 135, 0.12);
    color: rgb(var(--color-foreground));
    font-size: 1.35rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.2;
    cursor: pointer;
    transition: background-color 0.15s ease;
  }

  .aeonic-watch__submit:hover:not(:disabled) {
    background: rgba(231, 204, 135, 0.24);
  }

  .aeonic-watch__submit:disabled {
    opacity: 0.6;
    cursor: default;
  }

  .aeonic-watch__msg {
    margin: 0.9rem 0 0;
    font-size: 1.3rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .aeonic-watch__msg[hidden] {
    display: none;
  }

  .aeonic-watch__msg--ok {
    color: #2ea04d;
  }

  .aeonic-watch__msg--err {
    color: rgba(var(--color-foreground), 0.75);
  }

  .aeonic-watch__fine {
    margin: 0.8rem 0 0;
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: rgba(var(--color-foreground), 0.42);
  }
{%- endstyle -%}
